  "docTitle": "Palindrome DP and interval DP - SDE Prep Dojo",
  "description": "Deep dive: palindromic substrings by expanding around centres, longest palindromic subsequence and minimum insertions, palindrome partitioning II in O(n) memory, interval DP with a split point (burst balloons, cutting a stick) with the diagonal fill order, and egg drop, with steppers and Go/C++/Java/Python templates.",
  "hero": {
    "tag": "header",
    "attrs": {
      "class": "page-hero"
    },
    "html": "\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"5\">Level 5 - Interview-ready</span>\n    <span class=\"time\">40 min</span>\n    <span class=\"chip\">Deep dive</span>\n    <span class=\"chip\">Dynamic Programming</span>\n  </div>\n  <h1>Palindrome DP and interval DP</h1>\n  <p class=\"lead\">Some DP problems are not about a prefix but about a stretch <code>s[i..j]</code> in the middle. Palindromes are the gentle start: expand around centres for substrings, a table over (i, j) for subsequences, a 1-D cut array for partitioning. Then the same table with a <b>split point</b> k solves burst balloons, cutting a stick and matrix-chain style problems. The fill order (diagonal by diagonal) is where most bugs hide, so the steppers show it cell by cell. Egg drop closes the page as the classic \"think about the decision, then flip the question\" problem. Templates in Go, C++, Java and Python.</p>\n"
  },
